ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: yellow
MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS: [
 "phi<<0 on MATH is a near-tautological consequence of the answer-space geometry the canonicalizer itself defines: 'correct' is one gold value (low H_C by construction), 'wrong' is sampled from many distinct values with the same surface generator (high H_W by construction). H_C<H_W follows from |support_correct|=1 vs |support_wrong|>=3 regardless of any model behavior — this is a property of the proxy DGP, not an empirical finding about LLMs.",
 "The L0 'sign-flip' is the standard spoiler/Duverger result: under plurality voting, merging buckets shifts the winner in the direction of whichever side was more fragmented. Calling phi the 'governor' is just restating that plurality voting is non-monotone under bucket-merging. No new mechanism beyond Wang2022/Bulian2022 self-consistency + answer-equivalence literature.",
 "q=1.0 is unsurprising and not load-bearing evidence FOR the claim: sympy-Rational equality on gold-vs-gold pairs is exact arithmetic; 0 false merges among hand-picked distinct rationals is what any correct implementation must produce. This is a sanity check on the normalizer, not evidence the hazard manifests in the wild.",
 "Stage-B null is consistent with EITHER (i) the phi-governance story OR (ii) 'numeric canonicalization on GSM8K integers is a near-identity map' (only 6-8% bucket collapse). The null does not discriminate — it is predicted by both the proposed mechanism and the trivial 'nothing to merge' alternative."
]
CONFOUNDS: [
 "Surface-form generator is the same artifact used to compute BOTH H_C and H_W; phi is a property of that generator's parameterization (how many surface variants per value, how wrong-value support is sampled), not of any real model distribution. The +0.86 -> +0.26 shift on GSM8K under 'symmetric surface treatment' is the tell — phi is generator-tunable.",
 "MATH-500 H_C~1.15 vs H_W~2.0 is dominated by support-size asymmetry (1 correct value vs 3-8 wrong values), not by surface-form fragmentation per se. A model that actually concentrates wrong mass on one attractor (the spoiler-effect premise) would yield H_W near 0, not 2.0 — so the measured phi may not match real-model phi even in sign-magnitude.",
 "Stage-A 'correct mass fragmented across equivalent surface forms' (the headline mechanism) is NOT what was measured: with one gold value per problem and a surface generator, H_C reflects only surface-variant count, while H_W reflects value-support-size + surface variants. These are different sources of entropy conflated under one phi."
]
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED: [
 "That real model-sample answer frequencies on MATH exhibit phi<<0. The packet explicitly flags this as the open item; without it, the claim's load-bearing quantity is unmeasured on real LLMs.",
 "That the canonicalizer-recall axis (EXACT -> NUMERIC) corresponds to a meaningful intervention in practice — practitioners typically use one grader, not swap; the 'harness-induced ranking hazard' framing assumes graders are interchangeably deployed.",
 "Monotonicity-in-recall is asserted ('its sign is governed by phi') but only two recall levels are tested; intermediate normalizers (LEXICAL, recall 0.485 on MATH) are not swept to verify a monotone phi-keyed slope.",
 "That the L0 inversion z-values (-19.8 / +41.6 / |z|=48/53) are not artifacts of the post-hoc retune (0.42/0.46 -> 0.50/0.28) the packet itself flags as exploratory — no held-out replication of the L0 sign-flip is reported."
]
STATISTICAL_GAPS: [
 "Stage-B n=150 problems, k=16, single seed, single benchmark, single model family (Qwen2.5). No CI on the 0.480 vs 0.487 difference; no bootstrap on bucket-collapse counts; no replicate seeds. A 'null' from one underpowered run is weak evidence either way.",
 "Stage-A phi is reported as means/medians without CIs or per-problem variance bands; 'frac |phi|>0.2 = 0.93' is reported but no test that this differs from a permutation null on the surface generator.",
 "No paired-model variance: the inversion claim requires two models that differ in answer-surface concentration, but only one model family at two sizes is tested in Stage B, and only proxy distributions in Stage A.",
 "Adversarial precision (0 over-merges on hand-curated pairs like 18 vs 18.5) is anecdotal, not a randomized adversarial battery; q=1.0 is on gold-vs-gold not gold-vs-model-output, where free-form LLM strings could trigger sympy parser failures or silent passes."
]
RATIONALE: The packet establishes two things solidly — (i) a real numeric/sympy normalizer is high-precision on gold-vs-gold pairs (q=1.0, expected and not surprising), and (ii) MATH-500 gold answer-space has small correct support vs larger wrong-value support, which arithmetically forces H_C<H_W under any sane surface generator. Neither is a non-trivial empirical finding about LLM eval; both are properties of the eval setup. The actual claim — that canonicalizer-recall flips maj@k rankings on real models via phi-asymmetry — rests on (a) a SIM-only inversion that the authors themselves flag as post-hoc-retuned exploratory, and (b) a real-data Stage-B null on GSM8K that is equally well explained by 'numeric grader is near-identity on integers' as by the proposed phi-mechanism. The mechanism is spoiler-effect/Duverger applied to plurality voting over canonicalizer buckets — a known result (Wang2022 self-consistency + Bulian2022 BEM literature), and the packet acknowledges this is a novel domain-application rather than a new mechanism. Without a real-model phi measurement on MATH and a demonstrated in-the-wild inversion, the load-bearing causal chain is unclosed. The L1 ecological gate is real but only proves the foothold is not impossible, not that the hazard manifests. YELLOW: honest partial result, gated on L2 (real MATH model-sample phi + demonstrated inversion with monotone phi-keyed slope across >=3 recall levels and multiple model pairs / seeds).
